    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This charming and quaint two-bedroom mid-terrace home is ideally positioned in Cork City and offers a wonderful blend of character, comfort and future potential. Dating from circa 1900 and extending to approximately 83 sq. m., the property has been exceptionally well maintained throughout and presents in excellent condition. Retaining much of the charm associated with a home of its era, it has also been thoughtfully updated over the years to provide comfortable modern living. The accommodation is well proportioned and offers a warm and inviting feel throughout, with the recently upgraded kitchen being a particular highlight. The two bedrooms are well suited to a variety of needs. One of the property's standout features is undoubtedly the exceptionally large rear garden. Enjoying a wonderful westerly aspect, the garden offers an abundance of outdoor space and is a rare find for a city property of this type.  Located within Cork City, the property is ideally placed for those looking to enjoy the convenience and vibrancy of city living, with a wide range of amenities, shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and transport links all within easy reach. This is a delightful home that combines period charm with excellent presentation and an exceptionally generous rear garden."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall:\r\n3.75m x .80m \r\nWarm and welcoming entrance with access to all accommodation \r\n\r\n\r\nLiving Room:\r\n3.39m x 3.33m \r\nOverlooking the front garden, the room benefits from timber floor, decorative ceiling coving and fireplace with gas fire insert. \r\n\r\n\r\nFamily Room\r\n4.06m x 3.31m \r\nGreat additional living accommodation. Overlooking the rear garden, benefits from timber flooring and fireplace. \r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen:\r\n2.61m x 2.34m \r\nFully fitted with floor and eye level modern units. The kitchen benefits from tiled floor, subway backsplash, integrated fridge/freezer, breakfast bar. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom:\r\n2.07m x 1.87m \r\nComprises of three-piece suite with shower cubicle and fitted with electric shower. The room is fully tiled. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLanding\r\nAccess to all bedroom accommodation. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1:\r\n3.82m x 3.17m\r\nGenerous sized double bedroom, fitted with floor to ceiling built in wardrobes. Overlooking the front garden. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\r\n3.52m x 3.16m\r\nOverlooking the rear garden, double bedroom overlooking the rear \r\n\r\n\r\nGardens\r\nTo the rear, the property benefits from a substantial westerly facing garden, which is a particularly impressive feature for city living. Offering excellent potential for a variety of uses, the garden is predominantly laid in manicured lawn and is complemented by mature trees, creating a private and peaceful outdoor setting. A garden shed provides useful additional storage. To the front, there is a private courtyard providing a welcoming entrance to the property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming two-bedroom in Cork City\r\nExcellent condition with a blend of period charm and modern updates\r\nRecently upgraded kitchen\r\nExceptionally large west-facing rear garden\r\nConvenient city location\r\nAll mains services\r\nGas fired central heating"
      },
